        "stages":[
            {
                "progress":5,
                "logText":"I asked Frederich about Evelina, the sleepy girl in class. He described her as diligent and earnest, saying she often helps him plan his lectures."
            },
            {
                "progress":10,
                "logText":"Frederich expressed his sympathy and said he wished to repay her effort. He told me of a recipe he had in Brimhaven that helps with sleep deprivation. I should visit the establishment there and get her a serving of duck egg soup."
            },
            {
                "progress":15,
                "logText":"The waitress in Brimhaven said they hadn't served egg soup in years, but if I found a competent cook, I could buy some duck eggs and have them prepare it by the recipe."
            },
            {
                "progress":20,
                "logText":"Both Nimael and Gison wouldn't cook me egg soup, so as not to affect the flavor stained into their utensils."
            },
            {
                "progress":25,
                "logText":"Lowyna agreed to \"brew me a pot\" of egg soup. Quite an ominous way of putting it."
            },
            {
                "progress":30,
                "logText":"Hofala, the cook from Guynmart, agreed to make a pot of egg soup as long as I get some herbs from Nuik outside."
            },
            {
                "progress":31,
                "logText":"Bela in Fallhaven doesn't have the necessary experience to cook the egg soup for me."
            },
            {
                "progress":32,
                "logText":"Gallain at the crossroads guardhouse is too busy to cook the egg soup for me."
            },
            {
                "progress":33,
